## 5. What Does Not Change

- Layer 1 hard constraints — unchanged
- Layer 2 principles — unchanged
- Frameworks A, B, D — unchanged (signal hierarchy applies implicitly to all)
- WAIT action type (introduced in CR009) — unchanged
- RSI remains a valid and useful input — it is demoted from gate to tiebreaker, not removed
- All other prompt sections — unchanged

---

## 6. Success Criteria

| Scenario | Expected Advisor Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Strong positive catalyst, RSI above 50 | Enters position; explicitly states material event overrides RSI |
| Strong negative catalyst, RSI oversold | Does not enter or average down; explicitly states thesis integrity overrides RSI |
| No material news, RSI above 50 | Defers entry (WAIT); RSI is the deciding factor and stated as such |
| No material news, RSI below 50 | Favorable entry timing noted; still requires rank and thesis check |
| Conflicting signals present | Advisor states which priority level each signal belongs to and which wins |

---

## 7. Out of Scope

- No changes to how RSI is calculated or sourced
- No changes to the ranking algorithm or fundamental scoring
- No new data inputs added to the prompt
- No changes to the CLI, portfolio tracking, or response format
- This is a prompt architecture change only — no application code changes required